## Worksheet

**F1 — Core loop**: `Game` class holds all state; `SeededRandom` (seed-based, deterministic) used in `genMap`, `genPeople`, `fireEvent`, `spawnCaravan`; `endTurn()` resolves consumption→production→rest→storm→repair→morale→events→trade→win/loss in fixed order. Score 2.

**F2 — Map**: 8x8 `this.map` (64 tiles), terrain from `rng` in `genMap`; `canBuild` checks `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`. Adjacency bonus text is computed in `showTileTooltip` only — never applied in the production loop in `endTurn()`. Score 1.

**F3 — Economy**: `GREENHOUSE` converts water→food (works); `FORGE` consumes `ore`+`power` but `production: []` — metal is never produced anywhere in the code. Storage caps/overflow handled (`new_amt > cap` logic in `endTurn`). Core chain example is broken. Score 1.

**F4 — Population**: `people[]` records with `skill/fatigue/morale/job`; `output_mult` in `endTurn` reads `worker.skill` and `worker.fatigue`. Score 2.

**F5 — Needs**: `food_need/water_need` consumed each turn; shortage cuts `p.morale`; `if (worker.morale<50) output_mult*=0.7`; recovery via "Morale Boost" event and `morale-focus` research. Score 2.

**F6 — Research**: 8 nodes in `RESEARCH_TREE`; `queueResearch` enforces `prereqs` and deducts cost. `water-retention` and `ore-refining` effects (`water_cap_mult`, `ore_to_metal_mult`) are never read anywhere else — 2 of 8 nodes do nothing. Score 1.

**F7 — Events**: 10 entries in `event_list`; selection is uniform (`Math.floor(rng.next()*available.length)`), not weighted. All 10 events have 2 differing choices. `events_cooldown[name]=turn+10` blocks repeats until pool exhausted (crude but present) — never actually expires via turn comparison. Score 1.

**F8 — Trade**: `spawnCaravan` prices use `this.resources[item]/storage_caps[item]` (stockpile-driven); `caravan_inventory` finite and decremented/incremented; `tradeWith` handles both buy/sell branches. Score 2.

**F9 — Hazard**: `turn%8===0` triggers storm, `storm_severity` grows each turn, `storm-shelter` research cuts damage 0.6x, repair spends 5 parts and restores health. But production loop never reads `building.health` — damaged buildings produce at full rate. Score 1.

**F10 — Save/load**: `serializeState()`/`hashState()` exist but are only used internally by `devRunTests`/`devBenchmark`; no textarea, export button, or import parser exposed to the player anywhere. Score 0.

**F11 — End conditions**: lose at `people.length===0`, win at `turn>=60 && people.length>=12` in `endTurn`; `endGame()` computes score from pop/research/resources/turn and renders `#endGameModal`. Score 2.

**F12 — UI**: `switchTab` toggles `.active`; log entries show `T${entry.turn}`; `showTileTooltip` explains terrain/health/adjacency/buildable; keydown listener for Space + Digit1-4 (5 tabs, Dev tab has none); `@media (max-width:600px)` present. Score 2.

**F13 — Dev panel**: `devRunTests` checks resource bounds, health bounds, skill/fatigue ranges, prereq consistency, hash stability (mostly non-trivial); `devBenchmark` spins up `new Game()`, runs `endTurn()` x200 headlessly, prints `hashState`. Score 2.

**G1**: `research_done['better-farming']` etc. read directly inside the production loop in `endTurn`, multiplying `amount` before it's added to `this.resources`. Hardcoded per-resource special cases (dead `effect()` functions unused), 2/8 nodes have no hookup at all. Score 3.

**G2**: `food_shortage`/`water_shortage` computed in `endTurn` → `p.morale -= 10*(1-p.morale/100)` → `if (worker.morale<50) output_mult*=0.7` read in same function's production step. Full chain, threshold is a single hardcoded cutoff. Score 3.

**G3**: storm block sets `buildings[idx].health -= storm_dmg`; repair spends `resources.parts` and restores health — but production loop never reads `.health`, so output loss link is entirely absent. Score 1.

**G4**: `caravan_prices[item] = base_price*(supply_mod + rng noise)` where `supply_mod` reads `this.resources[item]/storage_caps[item]`; prices shown in trade grid and used in `tradeWith`. Score 4.

**G5**: Settler Arrival choice pushes a new object into `this.people` (durable); Equipment Breakdown choice mutates `this.storm_severity` ±, which feeds next storm's `storm_dmg_base` calc. Score 4.

